<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Abiove estimates soycomplex supply/demand.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Abiove estimates soycomplex supply/demand.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the May supply and demand estimate for soybeans and soyproducts in the 1997/98 commercial year (February/January), according to the Brazilian Association of Vegetable Oils Industries (Abiove).</p>
<p>All figures are in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p> SOYBEANS		 1997/98	 1996/97</p>
<p> Opening stocks	    550	     850</p>
<p> Production	     26,700	  23,950</p>
<p> Imports		   1,500	   1,100</p>
<p> Seeds and losses	1,600	   1,600</p>
<p> Exports		   8,500	   3,650</p>
<p> Crushings		18,000	  20,100</p>
<p> Closing stocks	    650	     550</p>
<p> SOYMEAL		  1997/98	 1996/97</p>
<p> Opening stocks	    347	     547</p>
<p> Production	     14,200	  15,900</p>
<p> Imports		     200	     100</p>
<p> Internal demand	 5,500	   5,300</p>
<p> Exports		   8,900	  10,900</p>
<p> Closing stocks	    347	     347</p>
<p> SOYOIL		   1997/98	 1996/97</p>
<p> Opening stocks	    195	     195</p>
<p> Production		3,400	   3,800</p>
<p> Imports		     200	     200</p>
<p> Internal demand	 2,750	   2,650</p>
<p> Exports		     850	   1,350</p>
<p> Closing stocks	    195	     195</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
</text>
